(vector (map (:db/id -1)
 (:adr/id "adr-2609112300-claude-md-under-the-agents-md-reader-limit")
 (:adr/doc_type "adr")
 (:adr/topic "claude-md-under-the-agents-md-reader-limit")
 (:adr/title "CLAUDE.md under the AGENTS.md reader limit — 115k chars to 25k, every moved section verbatim into a skill, and a generator that refuses to exceed the limit")
 (:adr/status "accepted")
 (:adr/date "2026-09-11")
 (:adr/deciders (vector "Jun Kawasaki" "Claude Opus 5"))
 (:adr/repos (vector "com-junkawasaki/root"))
 (:adr/related (vector "adr-2609081000-claude-md-holds-invariants-skills-hold-procedure" "adr-2609062600-agent-instructions-generated-from-one-source"))
 (:adr/body "## Context\n\nAn agent that reads `AGENTS.md` as a context file refused it: `Context file AGENTS.md TRUNCATED: 115347 chars exceeds limit of 31457 — trim the file, pin a larger context_file_max_chars, or use a larger-context model!`. `AGENTS.md` is generated from `CLAUDE.md` (ADR-2609062600), so the file to trim is `CLAUDE.md`.\n\nADR-2609081000 had already cut `CLAUDE.md` from 154,842 to 92,990 characters on 2026-09-08 by moving procedure and evidence into skills. Three days later it was back at 115,099 characters (44 H2 sections; measured with the section splitter used for this ADR). The growth was the form the document warns against in its own words: each new rule arrived wrapped in the incident that produced it, with dated measurements and tables that read as constants a week later.\n\nA reader limit of 31,457 characters is not a warning: the file is **truncated**, so whichever rules sit past the cut are silently absent for that agent. That is the failure class this workspace names in its eight questions — a rule nobody reads returns the same value as a rule that is not there.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **`CLAUDE.md` holds only what must hold without reading anything else, and must stay under 30,000 characters.** Every H2 section was rewritten to its rules — prohibitions, orderings, the one-line reason where the reason is the rule — and the narrative, dated measurements, tables and worked examples were removed from the inline text.\n2. **Every removed section was moved verbatim into a skill**, appended under a header naming this ADR, so the split cannot lose a rule by paraphrase. Destinations:\n   - existing skills: `west-pin-advance` (repository layout, genpon), `git-operations` (Git operations, parallel-agent operation, Agent delegation), `fleet-ci-gates` (CI/CD), `kotoba-authoring` (runtime priority, compile route, permanent-vs-temporary, whole-component migration, design-system 5 repos, JVM-free, resource governor), `kotoba-uiux` (UI/UX, 3D), `new-project-scaffold` (repo naming, no `-clj`, standing authorization), `build-actor` (Actors, LLM model alias), `large-binary-datalad`.\n   - six new skills: `verification-discipline` (the eight questions, before concluding absent, property-vs-implementation-state, base-library constant factors), `docs-adr-authoring`, `kotobase-planes` (the ten kotobase sections: L2 CID, app 4 planes, privacy, kotobase.net persistence, join reach, D1, datom-not-Datalog, three names, CARv2 pack + 5 IR, agent loop projection), `closing`, `human-authentication`, `business-loops` (direct-first procurement, system dynamics, BMC/Lean loop).\n   - the receiving skills had their `description:` extended so the new topics trigger them.\n3. **The generator refuses to emit an over-limit file.** `scripts/gen-agents-md.cljk` now carries `max-chars 31457` and exits 2 without writing when the generated text exceeds it. The fleet gate `root-agents-md-generated` runs the same generator, so a `CLAUDE.md` that would be truncated by the reader is red on the fleet rather than silently cut by the reader.\n4. The substitution table shrank to two anchors (`# CLAUDE.md` and the one self-reference in the Agent-delegation section); it still refuses with exit 2 when an anchor count changes.\n\n## What deliberately stayed inline\n\nEvery prohibition; the standing authorization and its seven-item safety floor in full; the eight questions as questions (one line each) plus the shell traps (`$?` after a pipe, zsh word splitting, `${r}:path`); every `before you conclude X` rule, since an agent that does not know it should search will not invoke a skill about searching; the kotobase plane invariants as one line per plane; the runtime order and the kbb-only invocation rule.\n\nTwo regions were rewritten rather than moved and are not in any skill: the preamble (the delegation table itself) and the evidence paragraph under `agent 指示は 1 本の正本から生成する`, whose facts (52 commits one way, 9 the other, ten `.Codex/` paths) already live in ADR-2609062600. The `secrets-location-map` pointer stayed inline as-is.\n\nOne dangling reference inherited from the old text — skill `nbb-to-kbb-migration`, which exists nowhere in the tree — is now labelled as unlanded next to ADR-2609081800 instead of being cited as if it existed.\n\n## Result\n\n- `CLAUDE.md` 115,099 -> 25,274 characters; `AGENTS.md` 25,515 (limit 31,457).\n- Containment was checked mechanically: every non-blank line of the pre-split `CLAUDE.md` (1,982) against the union of the new `CLAUDE.md` and all 42 skill files. 46 lines in neither, all from the three rewritten regions named above, reviewed individually.\n- Generator discrimination, measured before landing: unchanged source exit 0; source padded past the limit exit 2 and **no file written**; an anchor removed exit 2; output of exactly 31,457 characters exit 0 and 31,458 exit 2 (the boundary case the eight questions demand).\n- Fleet gate `agents-md-generated-check.cljk` run locally: exit 0, `SCANNED 3`.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- **New rules go in `CLAUDE.md` as rules. New procedure, evidence and measurements go in the skill.** The generator now enforces the ceiling, so growth past it turns the fleet gate red instead of truncating the reader.\n- The 25k form leaves about 5k of headroom. When it is used up, the answer is another move into a skill, not a larger limit.\n- Skills are read on trigger, not always. A rule whose trigger is unreliable must stay inline; this ADR moved none of the `before you conclude` rules for that reason.\n- `.agents/skills` (the Codex-side copy) is a partial, diverging mirror of `.claude/skills` and was not touched; the pointers in `AGENTS.md` name `.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` as real paths, which non-Claude agents can open directly.\n")))
